[00:23.820]Frozen whispers in the midnight air
[00:27.390]A fractured star with a lonely glare
[00:31.320]Dug from the heart of a silent year
[00:34.950]Something precious, something clear
[00:40.260]The quarry was a forgotten stream
[00:42.240]Where sunlight died a crystal dream
[00:44.100]I chipped away at the glacial wall
[00:45.870]To hear the ancient echoes fall
[00:47.670]My fingers bled a crimson stain
[00:49.650]Against the unforgiving plain
[00:51.480]A prisoner of eternal light
[00:53.460]Buried far from human sight
[00:55.440]They call it fire that cannot burn
[00:57.330]A lesson every soul must learn
[00:59.190]It holds the chill of a first goodbye
[01:00.960]And captures tears a cloudless sky
[01:02.760]It’ s not a gem for a crown or ring
[01:04.800]It’ s the weight of a solitary thing
[01:06.300]The core of storm where winds are tamed
[01:08.220]A brilliance that cannot be named
[01:09.990]Oh, ice diamond, cold and so still
[01:11.760]Cutting the light on a winter hill
[01:17.160]A perfect scar, a captured sigh
[01:19.710]Reflecting truth in a fractured sky
[01:27.750]时空重塑中~ iiiiii~
[01:30.000]It mirrors not a face, but time
[01:31.770]In geometric frost and rime
[01:33.780]Each facet holds a different past
[01:35.490]A moment meant forever to last
[01:37.110]The warmth of a hearth it will not keep
[01:39.150]It guards its secrets buried deep
[01:41.010]A monument to what’ s been lost
[01:42.810]Regardless of the human cost
[01:44.790]Oh, ice diamond, cold and so still
[01:46.290]Cutting the light on a winter hill
[01:51.480]A perfect scar, a captured sigh
[01:54.000]Reflecting truth in a fractured sky
[01:59.100]You burn my hands, you steal my breath
[02:03.030]A beautiful herald of frozen death
[02:06.120]And should I hold it to my chest?
[02:08.700]To put this chilling prize to rest?
[02:10.230]My heart’ s own beat, a feeble drum
[02:12.090]Would feel the coming numbness come
[02:13.890]To own this light is to be alone
[02:15.810]A king upon a barren throne
[02:17.670]Of glittering dust and breathless halls
[02:21.120]Where silent, icy shadow falls